course: dictionary
lesson: 4263
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which meaning you need. The word grave can be a noun, a place in the ground where someone is buried, or an adjective, a word that describes something serious or solemn.
explain: Look at the clues. In «visit a grave», the word visit and the idea of a cemetery tell you it is a place. In «grave danger», the word danger tells you it means very serious. In «a grave face», the face tells you it is serious and not smiling.
explain: Check your choice by putting the meaning into the sentence. Does «a serious face» make sense? Yes, so grave means serious there. Does «a serious grave» make sense? No, so the place meaning does not fit that sentence. Always test your meaning.
fact: Grave as a noun means a place in the ground where a dead person is buried, often marked with a stone.
fact: Grave as an adjective means very serious and worrying, as in «grave danger» or «a grave mistake».
fact: «A grave face» means a face that looks serious and is not smiling.
fact: In a cemetery, it is respectful to be quiet and not walk on graves.
fact: «Final resting place» means a person's grave, and «six feet under» means dead and buried.
exercise: Families went to visit a grave in the cemetery. What does grave mean here? | A deep hole for water | Very serious and worrying | Looking serious and not smiling | *A place in the ground where a dead person is buried
exercise: «The doctor warned of grave danger.» What does grave mean? | A place to bury people | *Very serious and worrying | Happy and smiling | Cold and wet
exercise: «He had a grave face when he heard the news.» What does grave mean here? | Very loud | A place where people are buried | *Serious and not smiling | Very quick and cheerful
test: «Making a grave mistake can cause big problems.» What does grave mean? | A place in the ground | Happy and funny | *Very serious | Quiet and soft
test: Which sentence uses grave as a noun, meaning a place where someone is buried? | «The grave news made us sad.» | *«We placed flowers on the grave.» | «The grave danger grew each hour.» | «She gave a grave nod.»
exam: «The old man spoke in a grave voice.» What does grave mean? | A place where people are buried | *Serious and worried | Quiet, like a whisper | Very fast
